# E2E Tests

Read and follow [`tests/e2e/STRATEGY.md`](../../tests/e2e/STRATEGY.md) before creating or changing specs.

## Priority

```text
1. Functional behavior
2. Dependent behaviors
3. Authentication and authorization
4. Persistence
5. Flows and redirects
6. Validations
7. Visual feedback
```

Do not approve a flow just because there is a toast, a filled form, or a URL change. Prove that the state changed and that the user can use what the operation unlocks.

## Structure

`tests/e2e/{domain}/{method}/{behavior}.spec.ts`

Helpers in `tests/e2e/helpers/`.

## Anti-patterns

```ts
// ❌ UI / feedback only
await expect(page.getByText("Account created")).toBeVisible()
await expect(page).toHaveURL(/\/signin$/)

// ✅ Operation + persistence + later use
await signup(page, user)
await signin(page, user)
await expect(page).toHaveURL(/\/projects$/)
await expect(/* authenticated area usable */).toBeVisible()
```

Sign Up in this product creates the account and goes to `/signin`; the authenticated session comes from Sign In. The main spec must cover Sign Up → Sign In → authenticated route.
